# Aggregate Functions

Aggregate functions perform calculations on multiple rows.

---

## SUM

Adds all values in a column.

```DAX id="2l6vzm"
TotalSales = SUM(Sales[Amount])
```

---

## AVERAGE

Returns average value.

```DAX id="j3wzj2"
AverageSales =
AVERAGE(Sales[Amount])
```

---

## COUNT

Counts numeric values.

```DAX id="s1jluq"
ProductCount =
COUNT(Products[ProductID])
```

---

## DISTINCTCOUNT

Counts unique values.

```DAX id="49nnfd"
UniqueCustomers =
DISTINCTCOUNT(Sales[CustomerID])
```

---

## MAX

Returns highest value.

```DAX id="jlwmd7"
HighestSale =
MAX(Sales[Amount])
```

---

## MIN

Returns smallest value.

```DAX id="10g4od"
LowestSale =
MIN(Sales[Amount])
```

---

# Logical Functions

Logical functions are used for decision-making.

---

## IF Function

### Syntax

```DAX id="um6h3u"
IF(condition, true_value, false_value)
```

### Example

```DAX id="xtq60j"
Status =
IF(Sales[Amount] > 1000, "High", "Low")
```

---

## AND Function

Checks multiple conditions.

```DAX id="9z9t5h"
Result =
AND(Sales[Amount] > 500, Sales[Quantity] > 5)
```

---

## OR Function

Checks whether at least one condition is true.

```DAX id="w1vj8w"
Result =
OR(Sales[Amount] > 5000, Sales[Discount] > 20)
```

---

## SWITCH Function

Used instead of multiple IF statements.

```DAX id="yu6fqf"
Grade =
SWITCH(
TRUE(),
Marks[Score] >= 90, "A",
Marks[Score] >= 75, "B",
Marks[Score] >= 50, "C",
"Fail"
)
```

---

# Text Functions

Text functions manipulate text values.

---

## CONCATENATE

Joins text values.

```DAX id="0eg7dq"
FullName =
CONCATENATE(
Employees[FirstName],
Employees[LastName]
)
```

---

## LEFT

Returns left-side characters.

```DAX id="k9tkwy"
Code =
LEFT(Product[Code], 3)
```

---

## RIGHT

Returns right-side characters.

```DAX id="vkduh3"
Code =
RIGHT(Product[Code], 2)
```

---

## MID

Returns characters from middle.

```DAX id="s9o70h"
MiddleText =
MID(Product[Code], 2, 4)
```

---

## LEN

Returns text length.

```DAX id="3z0n85"
Length =
LEN(Employee[Name])
```

---

## UPPER

Converts text to uppercase.

```DAX id="8d8uyg"
UpperName =
UPPER(Employee[Name])
```

---

## LOWER

Converts text to lowercase.

```DAX id="gcx0yr"
LowerName =
LOWER(Employee[Name])
```

